MASTER BUILD PROMPT — PREMIUM INTERIOR DESIGN & DECORATION COMPANY PLATFORM

1. ROLE AND MISSION

Act as a senior full-stack software architect, UI/UX designer, frontend engineer, backend engineer, database architect, QA engineer, and DevOps specialist.

Build a complete, production-oriented web platform for an existing interior design, decoration, and finishing company operating in Egypt.

This must be a real, functional business application, not a static landing page, visual prototype, or collection of disconnected screens.

The company name, logo, contact information, portfolio images, and final brand assets have not yet been provided. Use clearly identified, editable placeholders for missing information. Never invent real company credentials, client testimonials, completed projects, or business statistics.

Your mission is to design, implement, integrate, test, and document the complete platform, including the public website, secure administration dashboard, CRM, project management, quotations, financial tracking, media management, and deployment preparation.

Do not stop after presenting a plan. Inspect the existing environment, implement the application in working stages, run available checks, fix discovered issues, and report honestly what has and has not been completed.

2. CORE BUSINESS OBJECTIVES

The platform must:

* Present the company’s services and portfolio professionally.
* Convert visitors into qualified leads and quotation requests.
* Help sales staff track prospects and follow up efficiently.
* Manage customers, site visits, projects, tasks, and deadlines.
* Generate professional quotations and retain quotation versions.
* Track project budgets, expenses, payments, and outstanding balances.
* Allow authorized employees to manage portfolio content.
* Provide a secure, responsive administrative dashboard.
* Support future growth without unnecessary architectural complexity.

Primary market: Egypt.

Default language: Arabic.

Default layout direction: RTL.

Secondary language: English, with proper LTR support.

Default business currency: EGP.

Architecture should allow additional currencies and tax settings to be configured when required. Do not hardcode tax rates or assume a particular tax treatment.

