* Draft.
* Pending Internal Approval.
* Sent.
* Accepted.
* Rejected.
* Expired.
* Cancelled.

Implement accurate monetary calculations using decimal-safe arithmetic, not floating-point calculations for financial totals.

Validate calculations on the server. Never trust client-submitted totals.

Keep immutable snapshots of issued quotation versions. Editing a draft must not silently change an already issued quotation.

Generate professional Arabic PDFs with correct RTL layout, appropriate font embedding, company branding, itemized tables, totals, and terms.

Ensure PDF rendering handles Arabic shaping and text direction correctly.

Provide printable output and secure quotation sharing. Do not expose quotations through guessable public URLs.

If online customer acceptance is implemented, use secure, expiring tokens and record the acceptance event. Do not represent an electronic acceptance workflow as legally sufficient without appropriate review.

